[
  {
    "pkheadingid": 746,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Definition",
    "headingPosition": 1,
    "headingid": 576,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 115186,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 349,
        "headingId": 576,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Cystic chondromalacia is a degenerative pseudocystic lesion of the auricular cartilaginous plate.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-09-28T13:17:46"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 747,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "ICD-O coding",
    "headingPosition": 2,
    "headingid": 577,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 115187,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 349,
        "headingId": 577,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>None</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-09-28T13:17:46"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 748,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "ICD-11 coding",
    "headingPosition": 3,
    "headingid": 578,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 115188,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 349,
        "headingId": 578,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>AA41.Y Other specified acquired deformity of pinna &amp; Benign idiopathic cystic chondromalacia of the pinna</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-09-28T13:17:46"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 749,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Related terminology",
    "headingPosition": 4,
    "headingid": 579,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 115189,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 349,
        "headingId": 579,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p><em>Acceptable:</em> auricular pseudocyst.</p>\r\n<p><em>Not recommended:</em> auricular seroma; otoseroma; intracartilaginous cyst; auricular endochondral pseudocyst.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-09-28T13:17:46"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 750,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Subtype(s)",
    "headingPosition": 5,
    "headingid": 580,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 115190,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 349,
        "headingId": 580,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>None</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-09-28T13:17:46"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 751,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Localization",
    "headingPosition": 6,
    "headingid": 581,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 115191,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 349,
        "headingId": 581,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Ear helix, scaphoid fossa, concha, or triangular fossa {30470633}</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-09-28T13:17:46"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 752,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Clinical features",
    "headingPosition": 7,
    "headingid": 582,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 115192,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 349,
        "headingId": 582,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Patients usually present with a unilateral, fusiform, painless, slightly fluctuant swelling {1556479; 3755327; 5904038; 6508627; 15068513}; rare bilateral lesions may be asynchronous {2354120; 3083365; 6508627; 15068513}. Lesions present rapidly (&lt;&nbsp;12&nbsp;weeks) and lack overlying skin changes. A rare association with atopic eczema is reported, perhaps related to rubbing or repeated microtrauma {2354120}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-09-28T13:17:46"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 753,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Epidemiology",
    "headingPosition": 8,
    "headingid": 583,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 115193,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 349,
        "headingId": 583,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Auricular pseudocyst tends to be more common in young men (mean age: 35&nbsp;years; M:F&nbsp;ratio: 9:1), although either sex and all ages may be affected {1556479; 3755327; 5904038; 6508627; 15068513; 30564784; 30921629}. It has been described in all ethnic groups, although an increased incidence is reported in Chinese patients {1556479; 3083365; 5904038; 6508627; 15068513; 23575386; 30564784}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-09-28T13:17:46"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 754,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Etiology",
    "headingPosition": 9,
    "headingid": 584,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 115194,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 349,
        "headingId": 584,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>The etiology is undefined. Possibilities include ischaemic necrosis (related to repetitive minor trauma), abnormal release of lysosomal enzymes by chondrocytes, and an embryological fusion defect {3755327}. Trauma may be accounted for by contact sports, movement disorders (such as [Friedreich] ataxia, spasticity, or dyskinesia), or earphone or mobile phone use {1556479; 3755327; 5904038; 6508627; 15068513; 23473281; 26693094}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-09-28T13:17:46"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 755,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Pathogenesis",
    "headingPosition": 10,
    "headingid": 585,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 115195,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 349,
        "headingId": 585,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>IL-1, a mediator of inflammation, induces IL-6 (stimulates chondrocyte proliferation) and stimulates proteases and PGE2 production by chondrocytes, leading to decreased extracellular matrix formation, and thus may contribute to intracartilaginous cleft development {15341921; 21178846}. LDH isoenzymes are elevated compared with autogenous blood {23575386}, suggesting a disrupted cartilage origin {23575386; 26693094}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-09-28T13:17:46"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 762,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Macroscopic appearance",
    "headingPosition": 11,
    "headingid": 592,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 115196,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 349,
        "headingId": 592,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Lesions can be as large as 40&nbsp;mm (mean: 20&nbsp;mm). Unroofing procedures may show a central intracartilaginous cleft. Incision or aspiration may yield viscous, clear to olive oil&ndash;coloured fluid {3755327; 15235361}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-09-28T13:17:46"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 756,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Histopathology",
    "headingPosition": 12,
    "headingid": 586,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 115197,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 349,
        "headingId": 586,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>The cartilaginous plate contains a central cleft without epithelium (pseudocyst). The contour of the cleft may be irregular, associated with a rim of fibrous tissue or granulation tissue with plump fibroblasts. Mucoid material, haemosiderin deposits, granulation tissue, and fibrosis are variably present, depending on lesion duration or prior procedure {1556479; 3755327; 5904038; 6508627; 12619465; 15235361; 30470633; 25536139; 25255358}.</p>\r\n<h5>Differential diagnosis</h5>\r\n<p>The differential includes relapsing polychondritis, chondrodermatitis nodularis chronica helicis, and traumatic perichondritis.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-09-28T13:17:46"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 757,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Cytology",
    "headingPosition": 13,
    "headingid": 587,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 115198,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 349,
        "headingId": 587,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>FNA is sometimes performed, showing acellular smears of granular proteinaceous material {10945913}. Fluid LDH levels may be supportive in the correct clinical setting {30921629}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-09-28T13:17:46"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 758,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Diagnostic molecular pathology",
    "headingPosition": 14,
    "headingid": 588,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 115199,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 349,
        "headingId": 588,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>None</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-09-28T13:17:46"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 761,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Essential and desirable diagnostic criteria",
    "headingPosition": 15,
    "headingid": 591,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 115200,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 349,
        "headingId": 591,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p><em>Essential:</em> degenerated central ear cartilage, with a spectrum of haemorrhage, granulation tissue, and fibrosis.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-09-28T13:17:46"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 759,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Staging",
    "headingPosition": 16,
    "headingid": 589,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 115201,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 349,
        "headingId": 589,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Not performed</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-09-28T13:17:46"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 760,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Prognosis and prediction",
    "headingPosition": 17,
    "headingid": 590,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 115202,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 349,
        "headingId": 590,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Cosmetic concerns often prompt therapeutic intervention, to avoid infection, auricular chondritis, and further deformity. Recurrence is seen in about 1&ndash;5% of cases {15068513}.</p>",
        "timestamp": "2023-09-28T13:17:46"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  }
]